    "created_at": "2025-10-09T11:23:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-09T11:24:30Z",
    "body": "Dead `area` elements are not keyboard focusable in WebKit or Chromium (tested on macOS with \"Keyboard navigation\" OS setting enabled and Safari's \"Press Tab to highlight each item on a webpage\" enabled). Demo: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14146\n\nFurther, `a` elements without `href` are not keyboard focusable in any browser. Demo: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14147\n\nI suppose `area` elements with `tabindex=0` ought to be focusable, but they are not in WebKit: https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14148\n\nI would suggest to keep the spec as-is since it's consistent with `a` and matches the majority, and file bugs for Gecko and WebKit.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
