    "created_at": "2026-11-17T19:20:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T19:20:27Z",
    "body": "> The [spec for the <area> element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/image-maps.html#the-area-element) says:\n> \n> > The [area](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/image-maps.html#the-area-element) element [represents](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#represents) either a hyperlink with some text and a corresponding area on an [image map](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/image-maps.html#image-map), or a dead area on an image map.\n> \n> and also\n>\n> > If the [area](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/image-maps.html#the-area-element) element has no [href](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#attr-hyperlink-href) attribute, then the area represented by the element cannot be selected\n\nWhat do \"dead area on an image map\" and \"the element cannot be selected\" mean here?",
